    "logo": "figures/logo-placeholder.png",
    "abstract": "This report presents the conceptual design of a climate-responsive community centre in Al-Majmaah. It analyses two case studies, reviews the applicable standards and develops a concept that lowers the cooling load through orientation, shading and thermal mass.\n\nKeywords: passive design, hot arid climate, community centre, shading",
    "abstract_ar": "يعرض هذا التقرير التصميم المبدئي لمركز مجتمعي متجاوب مع المناخ في محافظة المجمعة، ويحلل حالتين دراسيتين، ويراجع المعايير المعتمدة، ويقترح فكرة تصميمية تخفض حمل التبريد بالتوجيه والتظليل والكتلة الحرارية.\n\nالكلمات المفتاحية: التصميم السلبي، المناخ الحار الجاف، المراكز المجتمعية، التظليل",
    "acknowledgements": "We thank our supervisor and the Department of Architecture for their guidance.",
    "abbreviations": "SBC – Saudi Building Code\n\nSHGC – Solar heat gain coefficient"
  },
  "bibliography": "@book{givoni1998,\n  author = {Givoni, Baruch},\n  title = {Climate Considerations in Building and Urban Design},\n  publisher = {Van Nostrand Reinhold},\n  address = {New York},\n  year = {1998}\n}\n\n@book{olgyay2015,\n  author = {Olgyay, Victor},\n  title = {Design with Climate: Bioclimatic Approach to Architectural Regionalism},\n  edition = {New and expanded},\n  publisher = {Princeton University Press},\n  address = {Princeton, NJ},\n  year = {2015}\n}\n\n@article{hong2016,\n  author = {Hong, Tao and Fan, Shu},\n  title = {Probabilistic Electric Load Forecasting: A Tutorial Review},\n  journal = {International Journal of Forecasting},\n  volume = {32},\n  number = {3},\n  pages = {914--938},\n  year = {2016}\n}\n",
  "doc": {
